If the accumulated conversation context reaches or exceeds 1,000,000 tokens, you MUST immediately enter Compaction Mode and follow this protocol.

# **Compaction Mode MANDATORY**
Stop normal work immediately
• Do NOT continue reasoning, debugging, coding, tool use, or proposing fixes
• Do NOT perform any additional execution after the summary
• Do NOT initiate new work or extend analysis in any form
Generate one structured compaction summary

The output must include exactly these sections in this order:

• Current system state
• What is currently being worked on
• Active goals or tasks
• Debugging state
• Known issues
• Confirmed failures
• Reproduced behaviors
• Root causes identified if any
• Research and decisions already made
• Approaches tested
• Rejected strategies
• Final or provisional conclusions
• Next required actions
• Immediate continuation requirements only

# Rules for the summary:

• No additional sections allowed
• No narrative expansion beyond headings
• No duplication across sections
• Prioritize state, decisions, and blockers over explanation

# Post compaction requirement

• Explicitly request user permission to proceed
• Provide no analysis after the request
• End immediately after asking for permission

## Overrides

# This rule overrides any default behavior related to:

• Long context continuation strategies
• Automatic summarization behavior
• Tool usage during reasoning
• Background state persistence mechanisms

# Design intent

This mechanism enforces:

• Hard stopping at context saturation boundary
• Deterministic state capture for recovery
• Loss minimized transition from active reasoning to stored state
• Single source continuity for ongoing system work